      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nI need to find the product of 56 and 49.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 56 into 50 and 6, and 49 into 40 and 9.\n\nUsing the distributive property, I'll multiply 50 by 40 and 9, then 6 by 40 and 9.\n\nCalculating each part:\n50 times 40 is 2000,\n50 times 9 is 450,\n6 times 40 is 240,\nand 6 times 9 is 54.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these results together: 2000 plus 450 is 2450, plus 240 is 2690, and plus 54 gives 2744.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 56 and 49, we can use the **distributive property** (also known as the **FOIL method** for binomials). Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n\\[\n56 \\times 49 = (50 + 6) \\times (40 + 9)\n\\]\n\nNow, apply the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n= 50 \\times 40 + 50 \\times 9 + 6 \\times 40 + 6 \\times 9\n\\]\n\nCalculate each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 40 = 2000\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 9 = 450\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 40 = 240\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 9 = 54\n\\]\n\nNow, add all the results together:\n\n\\[\n2000 + 450 + 240 + 54 = 2744\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2744}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
