      "text": "<think>\nI need to calculate the product of 84 and 66.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 80 by 60, which equals 4800.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 80 by 6, resulting in 480.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 4 by 60, giving me 240.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 4 by 6 to get 24.\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together: 4800 + 480 + 240 + 24.\n\nAdding these, I find the total product is 5040.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 84 and 66, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   84 \\times 66 = (80 + 4) \\times (60 + 6)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the distributive property (FOIL method):**\n   \n   \\[\n   = 80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 6 + 4 \\times 60 + 4 \\times 6\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part:**\n   \n   - \\( 80 \\times 60 = 4800 \\)\n   - \\( 80 \\times 6 = 480 \\)\n   - \\( 4 \\times 60 = 240 \\)\n   - \\( 4 \\times 6 = 24 \\)\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   4800 + 480 + 240 + 24 = 5040\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5040}\n\\]",
