      "text": "<think>\nI need to calculate the product of 79 and 98. To do this, I'll use the standard multiplication method.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 79 by 98 by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable parts. I'll start by multiplying 79 by 80, which gives me 6,320.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 79 by 18. This can be further broken down into 79 times 10, which is 790, and 79 times 8, which is 632. Adding these together gives me 790 plus 632, totaling 1,422.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together: 6,320 plus 1,422 equals 7,742. Therefore, the product of 79 and 98 is 7,742.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 79 and 98, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 79 by 98:**\n\n   \\[\n   79 \\times 98\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   79 \\times 98 = 79 \\times (100 - 2) = 79 \\times 100 - 79 \\times 2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part:**\n\n   - **First part:** \\( 79 \\times 100 = 7,900 \\)\n   \n   - **Second part:** \\( 79 \\times 2 = 158 \\)\n\n4. **Subtract the second part from the first part:**\n\n   \\[\n   7,900 - 158 = 7,742\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{7,\\!742}\n   \\]",
