  "object": "text_completion",
  "created": 1751294782,
  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Llama-8B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nI need to calculate the product of 99 and 81. To make this easier, I'll break down 99 into 100 minus 1 and 81 into 80 plus 1.\n\nUsing the distributive property, I'll multiply 100 by 80 and 1 by 1, then subtract the product of 100 by 1 and 1 by 80.\n\nThis will give me 8000 minus 100 minus 80, which simplifies to 7920.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 99 and 81, we can use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials). Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Express the numbers as sums of tens and units:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 = 100 - 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 81 = 80 + 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   (100 - 1)(80 + 1) = 100 \\times 80 + 100 \\times 1 - 1 \\times 80 - 1 \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each term:**\n   \n   \\[\n   100 \\times 80 = 8000\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   100 \\times 1 = 100\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   -1 \\times 80 = -80\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   -1 \\times 1 = -1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine all the terms:**\n   \n   \\[\n   8000 + 100 - 80 - 1 = 8000 + (100 - 80) - 1 = 8000 + 20 - 1 = 8000 + 19 = 8019\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{8019}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
  "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 22,
    "total_tokens": 443,
    "completion_tokens": 421,
    "prompt_tokens_details": null
  }
}
